.TH MONITOR 1 "PureC OS"
.SH NAME
monitor \- graphical system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B monitor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B monitor
shows CPU, memory, swap, network, disk and process information read from
/proc. It has six tabs: Overview, Processes, Resources, Network, Disks and
Settings. Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+6 switch tabs and Ctrl+Q closes the window.
.PP
The Processes tab lists PID, name, user, state, CPU share, resident memory and
thread count. Click a column header to sort, type in the filter box to narrow the
list, select a row and use End process (SIGTERM) or Kill (SIGKILL). Both ask for
confirmation. Processes owned by root are marked with a lock; their buttons are
disabled unless the monitor runs as root. The kernel enforces the same rule: a
user may only signal processes of the same uid.
.PP
CPU share is the part of the total processor capacity used by the process.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/monitor/monitor.conf
Settings, one "key = value" per line.
.TP
.I /usr/share/monitor/themes/NAME.theme
Built-in themes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/monitor/themes/NAME.theme
User themes. A user theme with the same name as a built-in one is ignored.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
theme
Theme name.
.TP
interval_ms
Update interval, 250 to 5000.
.TP
history
Number of samples in graphs, 30 to 600.
.TP
start_tab
overview, processes, resources, network, disks or settings.
.TP
show_system_processes
true or false.
.TP
sort_column
pid, name, user, state, cpu, memory or threads.
.TP
sort_order
asc or desc.
.TP
cpu_view
cores or combined.
.TP
units
auto, kib or mib.
.TP
smooth
true or false.
.SH THEME FORMAT
A theme file has lines of the form "key = value". Colors are written #rrggbb.
Empty lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Missing keys take the
Default theme values.
.PP
.B name
is the theme name and
.B light
(true or false) tells whether the theme is light, which selects a matching
toolkit style for buttons and menus.
.PP
Color keys: background, surface, surface2, border, foreground,
foreground_dim, accent, selection, selection_text, warning, danger, success.
.PP
Graph gradients, each with _low, _mid and _high: cpu, mem, download, upload.
For example cpu_low, cpu_mid, cpu_high.
.SH SEE ALSO
ps(1), free(1), kill(1)
